coaching.claim:
The core design of the OAP slot is evidence-consistent:
- a dedicated unilateral slot, because strength is task-specific and transfers poorly to the isometric lock-off;
- independent per-arm state, because cross-education transfers only about a third of the trained-limb effect;
- complete isolation from kg progression;
- rule-based demotion;
- one-arm negatives gated behind rung 4 with 5–8 s lowering.
These match specificity meta-analyses and practitioner elbow-safety guidance. The automatic demotion of both arms to rung 1 on 9/12 worked as the spec intended.

Compared with the programs the athlete has failed on, REF5 addresses each documented failure mode at the level of principle:
- squat frequency: 5/3/1 Krypteia trains each main lift about once every 2 weeks;
- per-session volume: nSuns runs about 17 sets of two main lifts per session, vs REF5's 10 in total;
- unnoticed TM drift: Tactical Barbell Operator has no routine feedback and relies on 6–12-week retests.
Its session queue, micro valve and no-debt rule also fit an irregular schedule: 14 Plan-B sessions at 2.45/wk, median 47 minutes, three 8-day gaps absorbed without manual action. Its nearest relatives are GZCLP, which cuts AMRAPs at a noticeable bar slowdown, and Sheiko-style submaximal practice. What it gives up versus 5/3/1 and Tactical Barbell is a periodic maximal reality check (see R5-06).
